Test-process isolation note
The four suites above pass in fresh canonical Python processes (106 total).
When integration and P04 are deliberately combined in one interpreter,
the integration fixture prepends the SGLang source tree to sys.path, so
importlib.metadata.distribution("sglang").locate_file("") resolves the source
egg-info instead of the installed wheel. Three P04 installation-identity
assertions then fail for that synthetic shared-interpreter order. The isolated
P04 runtime-identity suite and its read-only engine probe both pass 24/24.
